      "worked_solution": "We can calculate the surface area of a cylinder using the formula\n\n$$\nS = 2\\pi r^2 + 2\\pi rh,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nSubstituting $r=3 \\,\\textrm{in}$ and $h=9\\,\\textrm{in}$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi (3)^{2}+2\\pi (3)(9) \\\\  & =18\\pi +54\\pi  \\\\  & =72\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
